"""FM Radio: tune a V4L2 radio receiver (/dev/radio0).

A small GTK4/libadwaita front end for the kernel's V4L2 radio API, written
for the LG V30's WCN3990 receiver (radio-qca-fm) but not specific to it.
It tunes, seeks with the hardware seek, shows signal strength and stereo,
decodes the RDS programme service name and radiotext, and keeps presets.

Sound is a separate path: the tuner only demodulates, and the audio arrives
on an ALSA capture device. The app reads that device, plays it to whichever
PipeWire/PulseAudio output is chosen (so the speaker works while headphones
are plugged in as the antenna), and can record it to a file. Where the
kernel offers no FM capture device, the app says so instead of pretending.

The capture device is $FM_RADIO_CAPTURE if set, else the first ALSA capture
PCM whose name contains "FM".
"""
